WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.120
Even with a runtime of more than two hours,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:08.400
"Eternals" is still a dense movie, full of&nbsp;
exposition that reshapes the Marvel universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.840
Meaningful moments are dropped in with&nbsp;
barely enough time to breathe before the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:16.400
conversation turns. These are the lines in&nbsp;
"Eternals" that mean more than you realize.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.211
When Dane Whitman finally comes&nbsp;
face-to-face with Ikaris, the on-again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.211 --> 00:00:26.480
off-again ex-boyfriend of Sersi, things are&nbsp;
understandably a little awkward. For some time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:30.000
he's heard about his girlfriend's ex, and&nbsp;
it's never easy to live in the shadow of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.840
someone else -- especially when he's&nbsp;
got several thousand years on you.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.040
"How long were you together?"

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.240
"Five thousand years."

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.080
"I guess you could call that 'long-term.'"

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:41.200
Dane has been trying hard to&nbsp;
get past Sersi's recollections&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.960
of "the pilot" -- so nicknamed&nbsp;
because Ikaris can fly -- get it?

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:48.080
Now, as the information&nbsp;
finally begins to coalesce,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:52.720
the line shows that Dane is trying to play it&nbsp;
cool. He's trying to be supportive of Sersi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:56.560
but is likely feeling a bit inadequate&nbsp;
compared to the eternal being who can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:01.680
literally fly. After all, how would you feel&nbsp;
if you discovered your ex had dated Superman?

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:05.440
“Dad! That's Superman! With the cape? And you&nbsp;
were shooting laser beams out of your eyes."

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:11.520
Dane's question to Sersi about why the&nbsp;
Eternals sat out the whole Thanos thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.760
poses a question that many MCU fans have&nbsp;
spent time thinking about themselves.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:21.040
It also reflects on a hard-to-grasp reality about&nbsp;
these long-living, god-like beings: they're just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:26.000
middle management, made by the Celestials to&nbsp;
exterminate Deviants -- and that's about it.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.520
"We were instructed not to interfere until now."

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:34.960
When the Eternals were created and installed on&nbsp;
Earth all those years ago, they were given orders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:40.240
and they have followed those orders well. Humanity&nbsp;
has spent the last several hundred years thriving,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:44.720
both in terms of population and the development&nbsp;
of technologies and medicine. At the beginning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:49.040
of the "current day" scenes in the film, the&nbsp;
Deviants have seemingly been exterminated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:52.800
and the group have been rewarded with&nbsp;
a well-deserved extended vacation.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:57.600
As details of "the emergence" are revealed, it&nbsp;
should serve as a cause for celebration among&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:02.000
the Eternals. It signifies a job well done,&nbsp;
and although it means the end of humanity as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:06.560
we know it, for the Eternals it's the equivalent&nbsp;
of building a successful branch office and being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:10.960
promoted to go head up a new region. A few of&nbsp;
them are ready to take this pat on the back and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:15.920
help the bosses with new development plans; this&nbsp;
line shows how Sersi begins the film toeing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:22.160
company line, but eventually comes to realize&nbsp;
she loves her underlings at the local branch.

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:26.240
It's obvious early on that Thena is&nbsp;
grappling with some problems — and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:29.760
this line reveals the dark side of&nbsp;
that struggle. Through flashbacks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:33.280
we learn that the character is suffering&nbsp;
from something called "Mahd Wy'ry",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:37.840
which resembles what we earthlings typically&nbsp;
see in our elderly and would call dementia.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:40.080
Thena's eyes glaze over on occasion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:44.000
indicating an oncoming episode. She'll&nbsp;
sometimes forget where she is in time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.480
who she's with, and assume they must be an&nbsp;
enemy. This can be a very dangerous thing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:53.920
particularly with someone who has superpowers and&nbsp;
can manifest deadly weapons at a moment's notice.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:59.280
It is initially believed that Thena's Mahd Wy'ry&nbsp;
is the result of being alive for so long that her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:04.560
memories are becoming confused; as the audience&nbsp;
later learns, it's somewhat the opposite. Thena's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:09.760
problem isn't that she's forgetting things, it's&nbsp;
that she remembers everything. Unlike the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:14.480
Eternals, her memory hasn't been effectively&nbsp;
wiped clean with every new deployment; all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:19.280
these memories have become a jumble, to the point&nbsp;
where Gilgamesh needs to step in and serve as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:24.960
caretaker. But as it turns out, Thena knows enough&nbsp;
to remember the true intentions of the Celestials.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:30.880
"Find your own purpose — and one day, when&nbsp;
we see ourselves again, I want you to tell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:36.560
me what you've found." This line from Ajak drives&nbsp;
home the maternal role she has had in the lives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:40.800
of the Eternals for thousands of years — and&nbsp;
the mistaken moment when they believe they've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:46.320
eradicated the last Deviant threat from Earth.&nbsp;
As Prime Eternal, she is the group's leader.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:51.040
She has the greatest insight into the Celestials,&nbsp;
helps set the tone, and with these words sends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:54.960
the group on a long vacation where they&nbsp;
are scattered to the ends of the world.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:58.640
Kingo becomes a Bollywood star&nbsp;
in India. Sersi moves to London,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:02.960
becomes a teacher and falls in love. Ajak&nbsp;
finds peace on a ranch in South Dakota,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:07.440
Phastos settles in the suburbs of Chicago,&nbsp;
where he also finds love and starts a family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:12.960
Druig lands in the Amazon and uses his powers&nbsp;
to "protect" (or perhaps more accurately stated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:18.960
zombify) a village he comes to view as a utopia.&nbsp;
Gilgamesh and Thena have settled in Australia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:22.880
while Makkari seems to have stayed in the&nbsp;
spaceship and caught up on her reading.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:26.240
What would you do if you had several&nbsp;
hundred years of "me time" to yourself?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:30.320
What the Eternals choose to do says as&nbsp;
much about them as any line in the movie;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:32.960
it's a shame that Ajak never&nbsp;
got to hear their stories.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:34.560
"Pretty impressive, right?"

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:39.280
Possibly the most impactful line from the&nbsp;
film is the one where the Eternals realize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:44.480
that everything dies, except for them, because&nbsp;
they were never alive. It comes at a key moment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:49.600
when the Eternals essentially have the rug pulled&nbsp;
out from under them. For thousands of years they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:55.440
have been immortal, invincible, near-omnipotent&nbsp;
celestial beings; now, they understand that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.440 --> 00:05:00.960
they're essentially just worker ants whose hill&nbsp;
is about to be destroyed so they can start anew.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:05.360
The long-game of the Celestials was&nbsp;
known by a select few of the Eternals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:09.760
and each reacted to it in different ways.&nbsp;
It wasn't until the path forward became&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:14.080
clear to Sersi that someone became&nbsp;
determined to let it go no further,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.200
while possessing the ability&nbsp;
to actually put a stop to it.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:21.600
Where does the Marvel universe go from here?&nbsp;
Earth now has a group of super-powered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:25.200
somewhat-revealed heroes. Soon, they&nbsp;
might just help the Avengers save&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:28.640
the day — if only they can get&nbsp;
past their own identity crisis.

